title: Inter-Party Relationships
new-page: true
view-if: year <= 1932 and inter_party_relationships_timer <= 0
tags: party_affairs
is-card: true
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; inter_party_relationships_timer = 6;
card-image: img/weimar_coalition_2.jpg
max-visits: 12
#subtitle: Building relations with the other political parties of Germany.

= Inter-Party Relationships

The <span style="color: #C00000;">**SPD**</span> cannot govern by itself yet. Because we do not have an electoral majority, we need the support of other parties.

- @liberals: Strengthen our bonds with the liberal <span style="color: #FFCC00;">**FDP**</span>
- @conservatives: Strengthen our bonds with the conservative <span style="color: #000000;">**CDU**</span> and <span style="color: #286fe0;">**CSU**</span>.
- @spd_alone: The <span style="color: #C00000;">**SPD**</span> can stand alone for now.
- @easy_discard


@conservatives
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1;
go-to: cdu_coalition if cdu_in_government = 1 and spd_in_government = 1; cdu_op if spd_in_government = 0 and cdu_in_government = 1

@cdu_op
on-arrival: cdu_relation += 3*(1 - dissent)

We are currently in opposition to the <span style="color: #000000;">**CDU**</span>-led government, but that does not preclude the general building of feelings of good will.

@cdu_coalition
on-arrival: cdu_relation += 5*(1 - dissent)

We are currently coalition partners with them, so improving relations comes naturally.

@liberals
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; fdp_relation += 5*(1 - dissent)

The <span style="color: #FFCC00;">**FDP**</span> is the kingmaker when neither of the main parties gets an absolute majority, so having good relations with them is essential.

@spd_alone

Whether it is because we *cannot* or *will not*, we do not make ties with other parties at this moment.

- @return: Continue...
